# Rocket Trajectory Simulator

A Python-based educational tool for analyzing and visualizing
the trajectory of multiple launched rockets.

## 🎯 Objective

This project was developed as an educational tool to help
students understand projectile motion through numerical
calculations and graphical visualization.

The program allows users to define multiple rockets and
compare their trajectories based on their initial velocity
and launch angle.

## 🚀 Features

- Input validation for integer and floating-point values
- Simulation of multiple rockets
- Calculation of:
  - Maximum height
  - Horizontal range
  - Flight time
- Graphical comparison of rocket trajectories
- Custom rocket names
- Random colors for trajectory visualization

## 🧮 Physics Model

The simulator uses the equations of projectile motion to
calculate the main characteristics of each trajectory.

The gravitational acceleration is set to:

g = 9.81 m/s²

For each rocket, the program calculates its maximum height,
horizontal range, and total flight time from the initial
velocity and launch angle.

## 🛠️ Technologies

- Python
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Google Colab

## 📊 Visualization

The trajectories of all simulated rockets are displayed
in a single graph, allowing users to compare how different
initial conditions affect projectile motion.

## 📚 Educational Purpose

This tool is designed to support physics education by
connecting theoretical equations with numerical simulation
and graphical visualization.

It can be used to explore the effects of initial velocity
and launch angle on projectile trajectories.

